      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CROSS LOCKS (3) won again in quick time after running them ragged making it three straight, scoring by 2.25 lengths (24.66) at Sale over 435m. Looks to have an edge on most of these. HI BIG BEN (2) finished well back at Sandown last time when a 8 length sixth (30.45) but scored five back at Sandown (29.79). Has ability and can measure up. FLYING DOORMAT (1) tends to drift back and work into the race, finishing out of the placings two back before charging home into the minors latest when second (20.15) in a Grade 4/5 at this track last time. Has a strong winning record at this journey. Has a strong record out of this box with three wins and a minor placing from five starts. Can measure up. TOMMY THE HOOD (8) deserves plenty of thought over this distance.",
